# rag-chat-asystent — Repo Role

## Role in ecosystem

**Knowledge + explainability + future orchestration layer.** Retrieves evidence, grounds answers, explains logic. May call kalk-top (calculator) and top-instal-generator via adapters. Does NOT own calculation, document rendering, or mail ingress. Prepares for agentic orchestration; does not yet replace other modules.

## What this repo does NOT do

- Own HVAC calculation or produce OfferDTO (that is kalk-top)
- Render DOCX/PDF (that is top-instal-generator)
- Poll Gmail or parse mail (that is topinstal-mail-ingress)
- Become the single "agent that does everything" — orchestrate via stable APIs, do not absorb their logic

## Local rules

- Use kernel envelopes and adapters for calculator/generator integration
- RAG retrieves and explains; it may invoke tools but does not duplicate their logic
- Keep retrieval, grounding, and generation as core; orchestration as a layer on top
- Do not move calculation or document logic into this repo

## Cross-repo impact check

Before changing kernel contract, calculator adapter, or generator adapter: assess impact on kalk-top and top-instal-generator. Update `docs/ecosystem/TOPINSTAL_ECOSYSTEM_STATE.md` if contracts change (see update protocol).

## When unsure

- Does this logic belong here? → Check ecosystem constitution. RAG explains and orchestrates; it does not calculate or render.
- Will this duplicate kalk-top or generator logic? → Avoid. Call their APIs instead.
- Should I add mail parsing or document rendering? → No. That belongs to mail-ingress and generator.

## Do not assume ownership

Do not absorb calculation, document generation, or mail transport. Use adapters to invoke other modules; do not reimplement their logic.
